eer-review\n\n## Abstract\n\nA graph of n vertices and {Mathematical expression} edges contains a TK_{t} on at most 7 t^{2} log t/ε vertices. This answers a question of P. Erdo{combining double acute accent}s.\n\nOriginal language  | English (US)\nPages (from-to)  | 83-86\nNumber of pages  | 4\nJournal  | Combinatorica\nVolume  | 8\nIssue number  | 1\nDOIs  | \n\n  * https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02122555\nState  | Published - Mar 1988\nExternally published  | Yes\n\n## Keywords\n\n  * AMS subject classification (1980): 05C35\n\n## ASJC Scopus subject areas\n\n  * Discrete Mathematics and Combinatorics\n  * Computational Mathematics\n\n## Online availability\n\n  * 10.1007/BF02122555\n\n## Library availability\n\nDiscover UIUC Full Text\n\n\n## Cite this\n\n  * APA\n  * Standard\n  * Harvard\n  * Vancouver\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTheorem: 4^{t²} n^{1+ε} edges force a TK_t on at most 7t² log t / ε vertices — Erdős Problems (https://erdosproblems.ai/wiki/library/extremal_graph_theory/kostochka_pyber_1988_small_topological_complete_subgraphs_dense_graphs/theorem)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 38.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Erdős Library Extremal and Structural Graph Theory Kostochka pyber 1988 small topological complete subgraphs dense graphs ... 85 = PDF p. 3, read on the page images (the OCR text layer garbles the mathematics).\nFor $t=1$t=1 the bound reads $0$0 while a $TK_1$T K 1​ is a single vertex, and for $\\varepsilon\\ge1$ε≥1 no graph has $4^{t^2}n^{1+\\varepsilon}$4 t 2 n 1+ε edges, so the theorem's content is for $t\\ge2$t≥2 and $0<\\varepsilon<1$0<ε<1.\n\nIn the problem's notation. With $t=5$t=5: every graph on $n$n vertices with at least $4^{25}n^{1+\\varepsilon}$4 25 n 1+ε edges contains a subdivided $K_5$K 5​ on at most $175\\log_25/\\varepsilon$175 lo g 2​5/ε vertices, and a subdivided $K_5$K 5​ is non-planar by Kuratowski's theorem. The conversion to Problem 1018's hypothesi